[stderr] -## Product, personas, and outcomes
[stderr] +## Product boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Mock Fantasy Quest 4 is an original, small, single-player 2D fantasy RPG for a responsive public web application and installable PWA. A player explores one town and one dungeon, completes a short quest chain, wins turn-based encounters, manages a small inventory, saves or resumes safely, and reaches a short ending. The first release is useful without sign-in, remote sync, multiplayer, purchases, live operations, analytics, seasonal content, or player-created content.
[stderr]  
[stderr] -The first release is an original, offline-capable, 2D single-player fantasy RPG: explore one town and one dungeon, advance a short quest chain through turn-based combat and rewards, save/resume, and reach a short ending. Responsive web and installable PWA deliver the same shared game core; neither has exclusive story or rules.
[stderr] +The reference permits only the broad *party-based turn-based adventure* scope. All names, writing, art, audio, UI, maps, rules expression, and interactions are original.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Personas, jobs, and success measures
[stderr]  
[stderr] -| Persona | Job to be done | First useful outcome | Needs |
[stderr] +| Persona | Job to be done | First-session success | Product obligations |
[stderr]  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] -| Casual campaign player | Make visible story progress in a short session without a complex system. | Finish the tutorial battle, save, and know how to return. | Clear goals, readable choices, forgiving recovery, no required connection. |
[stderr] -| Returning player | Resume after interruption or time away without losing confirmed progress. | Load/resume and see the current quest context. | Checkpoints, save status, safe updates and storage recovery. |
[stderr] -| Access-needs player | Play the same campaign with preferred input and reading settings. | Complete onboarding with usable controls and understandable feedback. | Keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad where supported; text, captions, visual settings, responsive UI. |
[stderr] +| Casual story player | “When I have a short break, let me make clear progress in a friendly fantasy story without needing genre expertise.” | Completes the first battle and can explain how to save. | Clear objective, low-friction controls, readable state, forgiving recovery. |
[stderr] +| Adult returning player | “When I return after an interruption or a long gap, let me safely continue from meaningful progress.” | Resumes a valid save and knows what changed since the last checkpoint. | Explicit save status, deterministic resume, pause, recovery and update messaging. |
[stderr] +| Access-needs player | “When I play with my preferred input and readability settings, let me understand and operate every required action.” | Enables a relevant setting and finishes the tutorial battle. | Keyboard, mouse, touch and gamepad support; captions; readable text; visual controls; no timing-critical required input. |
[stderr] +| Offline or unreliable-network player | “When the network is absent or weak, let me play the installed campaign and protect my progress.” | Starts from cached content and saves locally. | Offline assets, durable local save attempts, clear disconnected state, no required online dependency. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Outcome measures for independent validation are: a new player can finish the tutorial battle and create/load a save; a returning player can continue at the latest confirmed checkpoint; and every release-one critical path is available on supported screen sizes and input modes when offline after a successful install/cache.
[stderr]  
[stderr] -| Journey | Happy path and outcome | Relevant alternate paths |
[stderr] -| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] -| J1 First session | Start → onboarding → town objective → tutorial encounter → win/reward → confirmed save. Player understands combat and saving. | Empty save list starts new game; invalid/missing content produces recovery UI; input changes retain actionable controls; cached game plays offline. |
[stderr] -| J2 Campaign | Load/new → town dialogue/quest → dungeon/encounters → rewards/inventory → quest completion → ending. Player completes the compact story. | Locked objective names prerequisite; empty/invalid inventory is explained; defeat returns to checkpoint; invalid state restores last confirmed save. |
[stderr] -| J3 Resume/recovery | Open → select confirmed save → resume → pause/save → return after interruption or update. Player loses no confirmed progress. | No save offers new game; corrupt/incompatible save is quarantined with choices; storage permission/quota denial keeps prior save and explains recovery; asset cache never overwrites save data. |
[stderr] -| J4 Target delivery | Open web or install PWA → set input/settings → play J1/J2. Same campaign works on supported surface. | Unsupported gamepad falls back to advertised input; declined install leaves web play; uncached offline asset asks for reconnection without deleting saves. |
[stderr] +## Core journeys
[stderr]  
[stderr] -Every P0 feature maps to J1–J4 below; no P0 feature depends on unresolved connected scope.
[stderr] +| Journey | Trigger and happy path | Completion / user outcome | Required exceptional paths |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| J1: First useful session | Open game → choose New Game → tutorial dialogue → move → initiate first encounter → choose actions → win → tutorial save prompt → save confirmation. | Player has won once and knows how to save. | Empty slot list; invalid/unsupported input is ignored with a visible hint; storage denied/full shows recovery choices; offline works from cached build; crash restores the last confirmed checkpoint. |
[stderr] +| J2: Campaign progression | Resume/New → town quest briefing → explore → acquire/use item → enter dungeon → win encounters → complete quest objective → return/continue → ending. | Player reaches the authored short ending with recorded completion. | Blocked route gives an intelligible quest hint; empty inventory and unavailable actions are explained; loss returns to a defined checkpoint without corrupting quest state. |
[stderr] +| J3: Save, resume, and recovery | Pause/menu → Save → confirmation → close/interruption → Load/Resume → validate snapshot → restore scene, party, quests, inventory, settings. | Safe continuation at a known point. | No saves offers New Game; malformed/incompatible save is quarantined and recovery starts from last valid checkpoint; deletion requires confirmation and is irreversible locally; simultaneous local/remote conflict is out of release-one because remote state is not a dependency. |
[stderr] +| J4: Settings and accessibility | Settings → adjust text/captions/visual/input/audio options → preview/apply → resume play. | Player can make required content usable without losing campaign state. | Invalid value is rejected and previous applied value remains; unavailable gamepad/permission is non-blocking; preferences persist separately from save slots; reset requires confirmation. |
[stderr] +| J5: Install, offline, and update | Browser visit → explain Install where available → install → cache a complete approved version → launch offline → receive update → choose safe refresh at a non-combat boundary. | Installed player can play offline and avoid losing an active session during update. | Install unavailable is explained; partial/failed cache preserves prior working version; offline first visit gives a recovery page; update never swaps assets mid-session; cache/storage failure directs player to protect/export evidence where feasible and retry. |
