[stderr] -## System relationship map
[stderr] +## System relationship map and invariants
[stderr]  
[stderr]  ```text
[stderr] -Authoring/validation ─packages─> Content (scenes, dialogue, quests, items,
[stderr] -                                encounters, localisation, art/audio)
[stderr] -                                      │                    │
[stderr] -Input + rendering + accessibility ─> Exploration ─interacts─> Narrative/quests
[stderr] -        │                              │                         │
[stderr] -        │                              └─starts─> Combat ─> Rewards/inventory
[stderr] -        └────settings apply to all player UI──────────────────────┘
[stderr] -                                                            │
[stderr] -                          Progression <──completion/reward──┘
[stderr] -                               │
[stderr] -Shell/session <──loads── Save/checkpoint <──serialises── shared game state
[stderr] -     │                         │                                   │
[stderr] -     ├─PWA cache/update────────┴─must never mutate────────────────┘
[stderr] -     └─error boundary/diagnostics ──> player recovery/support triage
[stderr] -
[stderr] -Release and quality validate every edge. Privacy/security constrain diagnostics
[stderr] -and any approved connected boundary. Account/sync, multiplayer, live operations,
[stderr] -and commerce remain optional interfaces outside the offline loop.
[stderr] +Content authoring/validation ──> Content pack ──> exploration, narrative, quests,
[stderr] +                                          combat, inventory, rendering and localisation
[stderr] +Input + accessibility ──> shell/navigation ──> exploration/combat/dialogue/settings
[stderr] +Exploration ──> encounter ──> combat ──> rewards ──> inventory + quest progression
[stderr] +Narrative ──> quest transitions ──> route/ending availability
[stderr] +All durable campaign state ──> checkpoint/save ──> load/recovery ──> shell session
[stderr] +PWA cache/update ──> approved content pack + shell; it never mutates an active session
[stderr] +Crash boundary ──> recovery record + player recovery UI ──> last confirmed save
[stderr] +Privacy/security + quality/release operations constrain diagnostics, storage, cache,
[stderr] +accessibility, compatibility and recovery across every arrow.
[stderr]  ```
[stderr]  
[stderr] -**Invariants:** a quest completion, reward grant, and progression flag persist as one transaction; an encounter changes party resources, inventory, quest state, and checkpoint eligibility only at its defined resolution boundary; save content identifiers validate against compatible content before resume; settings affect presentation/input rather than rules; and asset-cache activation can never delete, replace, or reinterpret a confirmed save.
[stderr] +Cross-domain invariants:
[stderr]  
[stderr] +1. A quest transition, inventory reward, defeated encounter, route unlock, and ending flag become durable together only in a confirmed save/checkpoint; a failed write leaves the previous confirmed save loadable.
[stderr] +2. An encounter consumes only an immutable authored definition and a session instance. Its reward is granted exactly once, recorded with the encounter/quest state, and cannot reappear after load.
[stderr] +3. Content identifiers, localisation keys, and save schema versions are stable within a released content pack. A load either migrates explicitly or fails safely without overwriting the source slot.
[stderr] +4. Settings and accessibility preferences apply to menus and gameplay but cannot change combat legality, quest completion, or save integrity.
[stderr] +5. Offline play depends only on local approved assets and local storage. Connected/account features, if later approved, cannot make the campaign, a save, or recovery unavailable.
[stderr] +6. Refresh/install/cache transitions occur only at shell-controlled safe boundaries; active combat and unsaved state are preserved or the player is warned before leaving.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Lifecycle boundaries are: authored data becomes immutable release content at packaging; content plus user choices becomes ephemeral session state at launch; only validated checkpoints cross into persisted save state; a loaded save becomes a new session only after schema/content validation; obsolete caches and deleted saves are removed only after their respective safety/confirmation rules.
