[stderr] +| Install | Browser-specific, not guaranteed | Install affordance where platform supports it | Unavailable installation is never a blocker to play. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## First-release completeness proof
[stderr] +
[stderr] +J1 is a complete useful journey with no deferred dependency: an anonymous player opens cached or online original content, starts locally, learns movement and turn-based battle, wins, and receives a confirmed local save. J2 then connects the same local systems through the single town and dungeon to the ending. J3–J5 protect access, readability, interruption, offline use, and safe updates. Account, cloud conflict resolution, multiplayer, commerce, live operations, and advanced analytics add no prerequisite to this chain.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Open decisions and explicit non-assumptions
[stderr]  
[stderr] -## Decisions carried forward
[stderr] +Before implementation/release planning, a product owner must select: engine/framework and vendors; exact supported browser/device/network/storage/performance matrix; authored content quantities and party composition; languages and localisation process; precise accessibility settings and conformance target; audio production scope; remote crash-reporting consent/retention/data-controller policy; account/sync conflict policy; multiplayer/safety scope; commerce; live-service ownership; and age/region/legal/store requirements. These are not silently resolved here.
[stderr]  
[stderr] -Implementation must not invent: engine/framework, repository/CI, browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, performance budget, update activation; party/content/balance counts; language/audio scope and exact accessibility settings; crash-reporting provider/consent/retention; or whether account sync, multiplayer, live operations, or commerce ship. Before any becomes a dependency, record its decision owner and its degraded, recovery, and deletion behavior.
